{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall sanctify.</b> At its entry the court sanctifies it, and they say: 'The year is sanctified' (Rosh HaShanah 24)." "<b>And you shall proclaim deror.</b> For slaves — whether bored through the ear or whether six years from his sale have not yet been completed for him. Rabbi Yehudah said: What is the meaning of deror? Like one who dwells in a dwelling — that he dwells wherever he wants and is not under the authority of others (Sifra; Rosh HaShanah 9)." "<b>It is the yovel.</b> This year is set apart from the other years by designating a name for it alone; and what is its name? Yovel is its name, after the sounding of the shofar." "<b>And you shall return, each man to his holding.</b> That the fields return to their owners." "<b>And each man to his family you shall return.</b> To include the one bored through the ear (Kiddushin 15)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:15.269086285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}